  "kind": "union of two censuses, taken at different hours of the trading week",
  "why": "A single census fixes the universe to whichever markets happened to be awake when it ran. The 2026-09-19 scan landed at 08:37 UTC on a Saturday - the quietest hour of the week for US markets - and returned an almost entirely Asian-session universe: KBO baseball and WTA tennis. A study running ten hours from there would spend its middle sessions with nothing open, and the emptiness would be an artefact of the census clock rather than a fact about the market. Unioning a US-active hour with an Asia-active one fixes a universe that has something open around the clock, and it is still frozen: it was built before session 1 and cannot move.",
